A component the build cannot inline -- `chain` is recursive, so it is its own
caller -- instantiated at a position no reactive slot governs. It is still an
instance: built once, placed once, never rebuilt. So the page carries a
`data-sngl-inst` anchor where the node was written, binds it as `__n1__pos`,
calls the factory into `__n1`, and appends the root it returns. That is the
reactive-slot mechanism minus the diffing a fixed position does not need.

The position is bound rather than looked up inline because it outlives the
instance: a `#[construct]` prop written from state destroys this instance and
puts a fresh one back here, and `__n1__pos` is what the rebuild's InsertBefore
names. Nothing in this program does that, and the binding is still the
position.

The handler is the other half. `d` is read by the instance's `n` prop, so the
click writes it through the setter the instance exports -- `__n1.__set_n(...)`
-- against the binding the build already made, not through a lookup.

Before renderStaticInstance the static renderer met the node and inlined the
component's body as markup. The body had already been flattened into imperative
statements for the factory, so the markup came out empty; the props and vars the
renderer mirrored into `state` on the way past were read before their own `var`
declarations, so each initialised from undefined; and the handler reached for
the instance by `querySelector('[data-sngl-id="__n1"]')`, an attribute nothing
carried, and got null.

	the static instance should have rendered [2]; body = "deeper"

deny out/none/html/index.html `data-sngl-slot` -- a fixed position is not a slot: nothing re-renders it, so there is no anchor for one
deny out/none/html/index.html `data-sngl-id="__n1"` -- the instance is the binding the build made; it is never looked up in the document
deny out/none/html/index.html `(?m)^  state\.__prop_` -- a factory's props live in the factory's closure, not mirrored into the page's state

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:app"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component chain(n int) ui {
    text(value="[" + string(n) + "]")
    if n > 0 {
        chain(n=n - 1)
    }
}

component App() ui {
    var d = 2
    button(text="deeper", @click { d = d + 1 })
    chain(n=d)
}

window(title="H", href="/index.html") {
    App()
}
